  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 2056(b)(7), a QTIP election allows the full value of a qualified terminable interest trust to qualify for the marital deduction, provided the surviving spouse receives all income for life and the executor makes a timely election. The entire $6,000,000 qualifies.
Wrong (A): The QTIP election is an explicit exception to the terminable interest rule under Section 2056(b)(7), so the trust is not disqualified merely because it is a terminable interest.
Wrong (B): There is no statutory limitation to one-half of the trust value. The QTIP election covers the full trust corpus.
