Wrong (A): A direct transfer of property to a skip person describes a direct skip under Section 2612(c), not a taxable termination.
Wrong (C): A lapse of a power of appointment may have estate or gift tax consequences but does not define a taxable termination under Chapter 13.
Wrong (D): A distribution to a non-skip person is not a generation-skipping transfer at all, since no generation is being skipped.$EXPL$
