-- Q5464: Estate and Gift Tax [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 2512, when a donor gifts encumbered property and the donee assumes the liability, the taxable gift equals the fair market value minus the assumed debt. Dawson''s gift is $500,000 FMV minus the $180,000 mortgage assumed by Vega, resulting in a $320,000 taxable gift.
Wrong (A): $500,000 fails to subtract the mortgage liability assumed by Vega, which reduces the net value transferred to the donee.
Wrong (C): $280,000 appears to subtract the adjusted basis ($220,000) from FMV, which is the gain calculation, not the gift valuation method.
Wrong (D): $220,000 is the donor''s adjusted basis and is irrelevant to the taxable gift computation under Section 2512.$EXPL$
