UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 6075(a), the federal estate tax return (Form 706) must be filed within nine months after the date of the decedent''s death. An automatic six-month extension may be obtained by filing Form 4768.
Wrong (A): There is no 60-day filing requirement for estate tax returns. The nine-month deadline is the statutory standard under Section 6075(a).
Wrong (B): Six months is not the correct period. The Code specifies nine months from the date of death as the filing deadline.
Wrong (D): The April 15 deadline applies to income tax and gift tax returns, not estate tax returns, which follow the nine-month rule from date of death.$EXPL$
