-- Q5481: Estate and Gift Tax [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 2056(b)(3), a survivorship condition does not disqualify a bequest from the marital deduction if the condition requires survival for no more than six months and the surviving spouse in fact survives. Chambers''s six-month clause meets both requirements since Adler survived.
Wrong (B): Section 2056(b)(3) provides a specific exception to the terminable interest rule for survivorship clauses of six months or less when the spouse actually survives.
Wrong (C): There is no statutory provision that reduces the marital deduction by 50% for survivorship clauses. The deduction is either fully allowed or denied.
Wrong (D): The marital deduction is not deferred. It is claimed on the estate tax return for the year of death, provided the survivorship condition is satisfied.$EXPL$
