-- Q5483: Estate and Gift Tax [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 2058, estates may deduct state death taxes paid from the federal taxable estate. The $1,200,000 state estate tax reduces Patterson''s federal taxable estate from $18,000,000 to $16,800,000. This provision replaced the former state death tax credit.
Wrong (A): State estate taxes do affect the federal computation. Section 2058 permits a deduction for state death taxes actually paid.
Wrong (C): The state death tax credit was repealed for decedents dying after 2004. Current law provides only a deduction under Section 2058, not a dollar-for-dollar credit.
Wrong (D): The state estate tax is deducted from the taxable estate, not the gross estate. It is classified as a deduction under Section 2058, not an adjustment to gross estate.$EXPL$
