  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 2042(2), incidents of ownership include any economic rights in a life insurance policy, such as the power to change beneficiaries, surrender or cancel the policy, borrow against the cash value, or assign the policy. If the decedent held any incidents at death, the full death benefit is included in the gross estate.
Wrong (A): The cash surrender value is a valuation measure, not an incident of ownership. Incidents refer to rights of control over the policy.
Wrong (B): Total premiums paid measure the donor''s investment, not incidents of ownership. Premium payment alone does not constitute an incident.
Wrong (C): The death benefit amount is the includible value when incidents exist, but the benefit itself is not an incident of ownership.$EXPL$
