UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 2010, the applicable exclusion amount is the cumulative dollar amount of taxable transfers -- both gifts and estate -- that is sheltered from federal transfer tax by the unified credit. For 2026, this is approximately $14.50 million per individual.
Wrong (A): This describes the annual exclusion under Section 2503(b), which is a separate per-donee exclusion that does not reduce the lifetime exemption.
Wrong (C): The applicable exclusion amount is a dollar threshold, not a tax rate. The maximum estate tax rate is a different concept under Section 2001.
