  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 6166, if a closely held business exceeds 35% of the adjusted gross estate, the executor may elect to defer the attributable estate tax. The maximum period is approximately 14 years: a 5-year deferral with interest-only payments followed by 10 annual installments.
Wrong (A): Five years describes only the initial deferral period. It omits the subsequent 10-year installment period permitted under Section 6166.
Wrong (B): Ten years with no interest is incorrect. Interest accrues during the deferral and installment periods at the special Section 6166 rate.
